WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.385
Welcome to L.A. Lasts A Lifetime.

2
00:00:03.425 --> 00:00:06.618
This short tour shows you how to find your
way around it.

3
00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:12.601
L.A. Lasts A Lifetime is an A to Z
encyclopedia of Los Angeles County,

4
00:00:12.641 --> 00:00:14.413
from Acton to Zuma.

5
00:00:14.453 --> 00:00:18.292
It describes 4,900 places: landmarks,
buildings,

6
00:00:18.332 --> 00:00:22.157
restaurants, shops, murals, homes and
more.

7
00:00:22.357 --> 00:00:25.576
It's organized like a reference book, in
two parts.

8
00:00:25.616 --> 00:00:31.329
Part One, the A to Z of Placenames, lists
the names of areas: neighborhoods, cities,

9
00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:34.548
unincorporated communities, historic
districts,

10
00:00:34.588 --> 00:00:37.678
and Historic Preservation Overlay Zones.

11
00:00:37.878 --> 00:00:43.194
Part Two, the A to Z of Places, is the
main directory of individual places.

12
00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:48.194
In both parts, you can browse alphabetically or
search for something specific.

13
00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:50.264
Let's start at the top.

14
00:00:50.304 --> 00:00:54.284
Beside the big number, the name of a
featured place keeps changing.

15
00:00:54.324 --> 00:00:56.361
Point at it, and it holds still.

16
00:00:56.401 --> 00:00:58.389
Click it to read about that place.

17
00:00:58.589 --> 00:01:00.840
A preview card shows the place's name,

18
00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.547
its neighborhood, its book number, and a
short account.

19
00:01:04.747 --> 00:01:07.301
Below is a sample of names from the book.

20
00:01:07.341 --> 00:01:10.478
Choose any one, and its preview appears in
the card.

21
00:01:10.678 --> 00:01:13.857
To read the whole entry, select See it in
the book.

22
00:01:13.897 --> 00:01:17.963
The site opens Part Two at that entry and
briefly highlights it.

23
00:01:18.163 --> 00:01:22.048
To come back, use the round arrow button
in the lower right corner.

24
00:01:22.088 --> 00:01:24.380
It returns you to the top of the page.

25
00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.088
Not sure where to start?

26
00:01:26.128 --> 00:01:27.936
Try the Surprise me button.

27
00:01:27.976 --> 00:01:31.428
Each press introduces a different place
from the collection.

28
00:01:31.628 --> 00:01:35.727
Show 200 more names deals out a fresh
sample of names.

29
00:01:35.927 --> 00:01:39.382
And Start at A takes you to the beginning
of Part Two.

30
00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:44.349
To reach Part One, select Part one in the
bar at the top of the screen.

31
00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:50.522
Part One has six lists: the full A to Z of
area names, L.A. City neighborhoods,

32
00:01:50.562 --> 00:01:56.379
incorporated cities, unincorporated areas,
historic districts, and HPOZs.

33
00:01:56.419 --> 00:02:00.368
The number on each button tells you how
many names are in that list.

34
00:02:00.568 --> 00:02:02.539
Select a button to switch lists.

35
00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:05.804
Here are the county's 88 incorporated
cities.

36
00:02:05.844 --> 00:02:08.468
The line under the letters confirms the
count.

37
00:02:08.668 --> 00:02:11.199
The row of letters jumps straight to a
letter.

38
00:02:11.239 --> 00:02:14.504
Letters in light gray have nothing listed
under them.

39
00:02:14.544 --> 00:02:18.477
Under each name, capital letters tell you
what kind of place it is,

40
00:02:18.517 --> 00:02:21.179
and which region of the county it's in.

41
00:02:21.379 --> 00:02:24.781
To find a particular area, type in the
search box.

42
00:02:24.821 --> 00:02:26.433
I'll type Echo Park.

43
00:02:26.473 --> 00:02:30.253
Echo Park isn't a city, so nothing matches
in this list.

44
00:02:30.293 --> 00:02:33.512
But the number on each button shows where
it can be found.

45
00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:35.298
I'll select the A to Z.

46
00:02:35.498 --> 00:02:38.657
Now look beside the name: a number and an
arrow.

47
00:02:38.697 --> 00:02:44.851
That's how many places in Part Two belong
to this area: 119 for Echo Park.

48
00:02:45.051 --> 00:02:49.471
Select it, and you jump straight to Part
Two, showing only those places.

49
00:02:49.511 --> 00:02:53.604
Find an area in Part One, then explore
what's there in Part Two.

50
00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:56.946
At the top, a chip shows the filter you're
using,

51
00:02:56.986 --> 00:03:00.558
and the line beneath it says how many
places were found.

52
00:03:00.758 --> 00:03:04.244
To remove a filter, select the small x on
its chip.

53
00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:09.202
Now the whole directory is back: all 4,900
places.

54
00:03:09.402 --> 00:03:12.238
To search by name, type in the search box.

55
00:03:12.278 --> 00:03:14.211
Results update as you type.

56
00:03:14.251 --> 00:03:16.903
If nothing matches, the site tells you.

57
00:03:17.103 --> 00:03:19.623
Check the spelling, or try fewer words.

58
00:03:19.663 --> 00:03:21.231
Watts has two t's.

59
00:03:21.271 --> 00:03:23.318
Now we've found Watts Towers.

60
00:03:23.518 --> 00:03:27.998
Reset filters clears everything and
returns you to the full directory.

61
00:03:28.198 --> 00:03:30.101
The letter bar works here, too.

62
00:03:30.141 --> 00:03:33.979
Select Z to jump to the places at the end
of the alphabet.

63
00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:38.346
To see one neighborhood or city, use the
box marked All areas.

64
00:03:38.386 --> 00:03:41.439
It lists every area, with its number of
places.

65
00:03:41.479 --> 00:03:43.758
Start typing to narrow the choices.

66
00:03:43.798 --> 00:03:45.582
I'll type K, O, R.

67
00:03:45.881 --> 00:03:50.050
Use the arrow keys or the mouse to pick an
area, then press Enter.

68
00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:53.251
Here is Koreatown, with 94 places.

69
00:03:53.451 --> 00:03:55.626
You can combine a search with an area.

70
00:03:55.666 --> 00:04:00.885
Typing Wilshire finds the places whose
address or description mentions Wilshire.

71
00:04:00.925 --> 00:04:03.569
Fourteen places in Koreatown match.

72
00:04:04.233 --> 00:04:07.871
Let's read one entry closely: the
Ambassador Hotel.

73
00:04:07.911 --> 00:04:09.410
First comes the name.

74
00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:13.361
Below it, in orange capitals, is the
neighborhood: Koreatown.

75
00:04:13.401 --> 00:04:17.340
On the right is the entry's book number,
A-092.

76
00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:21.039
Next is a short account of the place and
why it matters.

77
00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:23.054
Then comes the street address.

78
00:04:23.094 --> 00:04:27.465
Select it, and the location opens in
Google Maps, in a new tab.

79
00:04:27.505 --> 00:04:31.494
A small slanted arrow after a link means
it leaves this website.

80
00:04:31.694 --> 00:04:34.866
This label says Demolished: the hotel is
gone.

81
00:04:34.906 --> 00:04:39.910
The note that begins with Now, in italics,
tells you what stands on the site today.

82
00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.284
Some entries have a See it then link.

83
00:04:42.324 --> 00:04:48.045
It opens a historical photograph on Martin
Turnbull's website, also in a new tab.

84
00:04:48.245 --> 00:04:51.793
At the bottom is the category: here,
Historic Site.

85
00:04:51.993 --> 00:04:57.294
Other labels you'll see include Closed,
Probably closed, Partly closed,

86
00:04:57.334 --> 00:05:03.161
Site only, Renamed, Moved, New use, and
Damaged or Lost in the 2025 fires.

87
00:05:03.201 --> 00:05:05.212
Each one is spelled out in words.

88
00:05:05.252 --> 00:05:08.171
A place with no label isn't guaranteed to
be open,

89
00:05:08.211 --> 00:05:10.928
so it's worth checking before you visit.

90
00:05:11.128 --> 00:05:13.505
Some addresses are marked Locator.

91
00:05:13.545 --> 00:05:18.163
They give cross streets or a general
location, not an exact street number.

92
00:05:18.203 --> 00:05:20.493
A few addresses are marked unverified,

93
00:05:20.533 --> 00:05:25.358
and the street addresses of some private
homes are deliberately left out.

94
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.201
As you scroll, a bar stays at the top of
the screen.

95
00:05:29.241 --> 00:05:31.551
The underline shows which part you're in.

96
00:05:31.591 --> 00:05:35.972
Beside it are the number of places
showing, and a Reset filters button.

97
00:05:36.172 --> 00:05:39.714
In the letter bar, a dark square marks the
letter you're reading.

98
00:05:39.914 --> 00:05:42.290
Everything also works from the keyboard.

99
00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:45.371
Press Tab to move from one control to the
next.

100
00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:47.604
A dark outline shows where you are.

101
00:05:47.804 --> 00:05:51.727
In the area box, the up and down arrow
keys move through the list.

102
00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:53.270
Escape closes it.

103
00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:56.386
Type a few letters, and Enter chooses an
area.

104
00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:02.145
On a phone, the page rearranges itself
into a single column with larger text.

105
00:06:02.185 --> 00:06:06.564
The search box, the area box, and the
letter bar sit together at the top,

106
00:06:06.604 --> 00:06:09.679
so you can search and browse with your
thumb.

107
00:06:09.967 --> 00:06:14.039
If your device is set to reduce motion,
the site respects that.

108
00:06:14.079 --> 00:06:17.989
The opening number doesn't count up, the
featured name stays still,

109
00:06:18.029 --> 00:06:20.974
and jumps happen instantly, without
gliding.

110
00:06:21.174 --> 00:06:24.964
And if your device uses dark mode, the
site follows it.

111
00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:29.211
From Acton to Zuma, there's a lot to
discover.

112
00:06:29.251 --> 00:06:32.439
Start exploring L.A. Lasts A Lifetime.

